{
 "id": "pegboard-hammer-holder-pla",
 "batch": 3,
 "brief": "A hammer holder for a 1/4 inch pegboard (6.35 mm holes on a 25.4 mm grid, board 5 mm thick), PLA on FDM, printed on its side so the layers stack along X. The board's front face is the plane y = 0 (board from y = -5 to 0). An upper peg (5.8 mm) goes through the hole at x = 0, z = 0 and hooks down 9 mm behind the board; a straight lower peg goes into the hole at z = -25.4 to stop it turning. The holder stays in front of the board inside x = -25 to 25, y = 0 to 70, z = -35 to 10. The hammer hangs head up with its 30 mm handle through a 34 mm wide slot open at the front (x = -17 to 17, from y = 30 outwards), its head resting on the two prongs either side. Dropping the 1 kg head in puts up to 30 N down on the prong tops; knocking it puts 20 N sideways (X) either way. Safety factor 2.",
